<title>SOUTH KOREA: TABLE-N.Korean 1996 GDP detailed by Seoul.</title>
<headline>TABLE-N.Korean 1996 GDP detailed by Seoul.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are details of North Korean economic data estimated by South Korea's Bank of Korea:</p>
<p>NORTH KOREA'S OUTPUT GROWTH BY SECTOR IN CALENDAR 1996</p>
<p>(yr-on-yr percentage change)</p>
<p>					   1994    1995    1996</p>
<p>    Gross domestic product	 -1.8    -4.6    -3.7</p>
<p>    Farm/forestry/fisheries	 2.7   -10.5     1.0</p>
<p>    Mining/manufacturing	   -4.2    -4.6    -9.6</p>
<p>	Mining			   -5.5    -2.3   -11.8</p>
<p>	Manufacturing		  -3.8    -5.3    -8.9</p>
<p>    Construction		    -26.9    -3.2   -11.8</p>
<p>    Service			     2.2     1.5     0.8</p>
<p>COMPARISON OF NORTH AND SOUTH KOREAN ECONOMIES IN 1996</p>
<p>					  N.Korea     S.Korea</p>
<p>    Population (1,000)	     23,558	45,545</p>
<p>    Per-capita GNP (US$)		910	10,548</p>
<p>    GDP growth (pct)		   -3.7	   7.1</p>
<p>    Exports (FOB, US$billion)	0.73	129.72</p>
<p>    Imports (CIF, US$billion)	1.25	150.34</p>
<p>    Foreign debt (US$billion)     12.0	 104.47</p>
<p>NOTE: North Korea does not release economic statistics.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
